{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>איש (a man)</b> — It is possible to construe for it: accusations, that he not be established in the land. And the meaning: dwell in a settled place." "<b>יצודנו (will hunt him)</b> — He hunts his soul to be shoved, so that the men of his land shove him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 140, :notes {0 "The Hebrew of the second sentence is elliptical; translated hyper-literally. The implied subject is unclear.", 1 "The word למדחפות is a rare hapax-like form; translated hyper-literally as 'to be shoved,' matching the gloss that follows."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:23.565302568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}